# NSG Phase 2c (radio) — AMC + HARQ shipped; scheduler, TDD split, MIMO and
# multi-band audited and NOT shipped, with the reason for each.
#
# Completes Phase 2c together with antenna-2c.patch. The roadmap item read
# "Antenna model -> engine; TDD frame format + UL/DL split; AMC / HARQ /
# scheduler choice; MIMO / CA; multi-band + inter-freq HO". Two of those five
# are real levers in this engine. The other three are not, for three DIFFERENT
# reasons, and lumping them together as "won't do" is what hid the antenna one
# for two weeks.
#
# ── SHIPPED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * settings.amc_model -> --ns3::MmWaveAmc::AmcModel (ErrorModel | ShannonModel)
#   + settings.amc_target_ber -> --ns3::MmWaveAmc::Ber.
#   MEASURED: 6.98 -> 3.48 Mbps/UE (-50.1%) switching to ShannonModel. Note the
#   DIRECTION: Shannon is LOWER here, not higher. It is a capacity bound at the
#   target BER (1e-5 by default), which is more conservative than the error
#   model's BLER-driven lookup in the real 3GPP MCS tables. Useful as a
#   different operating point, not as an "optimistic upper bound".
# * settings.harq_enabled -> harqEnabled, settings.harq_processes ->
#   numHarqProcess. Both had to become GlobalValues rather than the usual
#   --ns3::X::Y route: the scenario Config::SetDefault's
#   MmWaveHelper::HarqEnabled and MmWavePhyMacCommon::NumHarqProcess AFTER
#   cmd.Parse, so a command-line value was silently overwritten. NumHarqProcess
#   was a hardcoded 100.
#   MEASURED: HARQ off = 6.98 -> 8.32 Mbps/UE (+19.2%). Higher WITHOUT HARQ,
#   which is right for a link this healthy — the retransmission machinery costs
#   resources it does not earn back. The engine now prints
#   "[NSG] HARQ on|off, N processes" so the setting is verifiable from the log.
# * settings.harq_processes is PLUMBING-VERIFIED ONLY: 8 vs 100 processes
#   reached the engine (confirmed in the log) but moved throughput 6.98 -> 6.88
#   Mbps/UE, inside the ~10% noise floor. At this scale a UE never has 100
#   outstanding processes, so the ceiling does not bind. No claim is made that
#   it changes behaviour here.
#
# ── AUDITED, NOT SHIPPED — three different reasons ─────────────────────────
# 1. SCHEDULER CHOICE — the alternatives are DEAD CODE, measured twice.
#    The fork ships MmWaveFlexTtiPfMacScheduler,
#    MmWaveFlexTtiMaxRateMacScheduler and MmWaveFlexTtiMaxWeightMacScheduler
#    beside the default MmWaveFlexTtiMacScheduler. Substituted via
#    --ns3::MmWaveHelper::Scheduler:
#      Pf       -> run "ok", E2 connects, log has NO error, 0 PRB, 0 throughput
#      MaxRate  -> same, 0 PRB, 0 throughput
#      MaxWeight-> ns-3 aborts
#    So exposing the choice would let a config produce a healthy-LOOKING run
#    that carries nothing. There is deliberately NO settings.scheduler field;
#    the engine API still honours NSG_SCHEDULER for research. Second reason to
#    stay on flex-TTI: the Level-6 slice-quota enforcement lives only in that
#    scheduler (SetNsgSliceQuota is a static, so with any other scheduler it
#    stores a number nobody reads) — the scenario now WARNS when quotas are
#    configured with a different scheduler instead of failing silently.
#    test_radio_2c.py asserts the BROKEN state, so a fork update that repairs
#    them shows up as a test failure telling you the field can be exposed.
#
# 2. TDD FRAME FORMAT / UL-DL SPLIT — not a lever BY DESIGN, not by omission.
#    This engine's MAC is flexible-TTI: MmWaveFlexTtiMacScheduler derives the
#    DL and UL symbol counts from demand every slot (m_maxDlSymbols /
#    m_maxUlSymbols with a deficit loop), so there is no fixed TDD pattern to
#    configure. The nearest real knob is MmWaveFlexTtiMacScheduler::SymPerSlot,
#    the TTI granularity — not the same thing, and not exposed. A VIAVI-style
#    "DDDSU" frame-format field would be a fiction here.
#
# 3. MIMO / CA and MULTI-BAND / INTER-FREQ HO — real architectural limits.
#    * No layer/rank/port handling exists anywhere in the mmWave PHY
#      (mmwave-spectrum-phy.cc, mmwave-enb-phy.cc): single stream. The
#      UniformPlanarArray NumVerticalPorts/IsDualPolarized attributes are the
#      antenna module's, and the PHY never reads them.
#    * MmWaveHelper does expose UseCa / NumberOfComponentCarriers /
#      EnbComponentCarrierManager, so CA is not structurally absent — but it is
#      untested here and the scenario is single-CC throughout.
#    * Centre frequency is ONE global value:
#      Config::SetDefault("ns3::MmWavePhyMacCommon::CenterFreq"). Per-cell
#      carriers need a per-device PhyMacCommon plus a separate channel and
#      propagation model per band. This half of the 2026-07-14 "WON'T DO"
#      verdict STANDS; only its antenna half was wrong (antenna-2c.patch).
#
# ── Verified (2026-07-26, engines/nsoran/test_radio_2c.py) ──────────────────
# 7 runs, PASS: shipped variants all carry traffic; HARQ enable and process
# count both reach the engine and are visible in its log; HARQ off +19.2% and
# Shannon AMC -50.1% both clear the noise floor; the three dead schedulers are
# still dead (0 / 0 / crash), reproduced across two independent sweeps.
